## SQ-CAL-01 | calendar loads, first-boot moved-keys WARN, mixins
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep -E "\[creativecalendar\]\|creativecalendar.mixins.json" logs/latest.log`; `grep -E "from creativecalendar.mixins.json" logs/debug.log \| wc -l`
@pass `[creativecalendar] time, seasons and crop seasons loaded`; no `still has keys that moved` WARN (the migration replaced it, 2026-11-03; on a CE file that still holds the keys: `[creativecalendar] took N moved keys out of ...`); no mixin apply error; debug.log mixes the 10 common mixins (CropSeasonGrowHook only where IE, The Dirty Stuff or Nether's Delight is loaded)
@fails Jar missing, Creative Common still holding `time/` (duplicate `/ccaltime`, mixins applied twice), or a gate id wrong in `CalendarMixinPlugin`
@from batches/r1101/cs1_split.qb
bootexpect \[creativecalendar\] time, seasons and crop seasons loaded
bootexpect still has keys that moved to config/creativecalendar-common.toml
bootreject creativecalendar\.mixins\.json.*(Error|error|failed)
shell grep -c "from creativecalendar.mixins.json" logs/debug.log; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z]* from creativecalendar.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sort -u
look debug.log mixes 10 common mixins (CropSeasonGrowHook only with IE / Dirty Stuff / Nether's Delight)

## SQ-CAL-02 | config split (first half; restart half in cs1b)
@group A
@commands Same boot: open `config/creativecalendar-common.toml` and `config/creativeengineering-common.toml`; restart once and repeat the grep of SQ-CAL-01. Migration (plan_scratch_bugfix_1103 7.7): before a second boot, copy the server's old `creativeengineering-common.toml` (with `[time]`, `[seasons]`, `[crop_seasons]`) into `config/`, set `[time.day] dayMinutes` in it to a non-default value, delete `creativecalendar-common.toml`, boot
@pass Calendar file has `[seasons]`, `[crop_seasons]` (with `grassOffPenalty = 0.5`), `[time]` (`.day`, `.seasons`, `.wine`, `.wine.boosts`), `[perf] seasonsMeltIntervalTicks = 4`, `[wthit] cropSeasons`, `cropOutOfSeason`, the values unchanged; the CE file has none of them; migration boot: `[creativecalendar] took N moved keys out of ...` and `moved edited values into config/creativecalendar-common.toml: [time.day.dayMinutes = <n>]`, the new file holds that value with its comments, the CE file lost the sections; a further boot logs neither line
@fails `CalendarConfigMigration` not run (no `took` line), edited value lost (default written), or comments gone from the new file
@from batches/r1101/cs1_split.qb
shell grep -nE "^\s*\[" config/creativecalendar-common.toml; grep -n "seasonsMeltIntervalTicks\|cropSeasons\|cropOutOfSeason" config/creativecalendar-common.toml; echo CE:; grep -nE "^\[(seasons|time|crop_seasons)\]" config/creativeengineering-common.toml || echo "CE has no calendar sections"
look calendar file has [seasons], [crop_seasons], [time.*], [perf] seasonsMeltIntervalTicks = 4, [wthit]; CE file lost them

## SQ-CAL-03 | script pack order and calendar scripts
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "startup script packs in order\|creativecalendar\]" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass pack order lists `creativecalendar` before `creativedelight` and `creativebrewing`; `[creativecalendar] core finished`; server.log `[creativecalendar] server scripts ready, features on: seasons, crop_seasons, time`; no `global.CAL missing`
@fails `kubejs_startup/creativecalendar/` not in the jar, or the mods.toml AFTER order not applied
@from batches/r1101/cs1_split.qb
shell grep -E "startup script packs in order|creativecalendar\]|global.CAL missing" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log
kjsexpect \[creativecalendar\] server scripts ready, features on: seasons, crop_seasons, time
kjsreject global\.CAL missing
look pack order lists creativecalendar before creativedelight and creativebrewing; core finished line present

## SQ-CAL-04 | /cetime commands
@group A
@commands `/ccaltime`; `/ccaltime push`; `/ccaltime date`; grep latest.log for `[time] Better Days from [time]`
@pass `/ccaltime` prints the derived values (day 45 + night 15 min, 8 days per sub-season, preset SINGLEPLAYER); push and date answer as before (SQ-TD-01 format); the server-start push line is there
@fails `TimeCommand` / `TimePush` not registered (CreativeCalendar constructor)
@from batches/r1101/cs1_split.qb
bootexpect \[time\] Better Days from \[time\]
> cetime
> cetime push
> cetime date
reject Unknown command
expect 45
look /cetime shows day 45 + night 15 min, 8 days per sub-season, preset SINGLEPLAYER; push and date answer in SQ-TD-01 format

## SQ-CAL-05 | season clock follows the sun
@group A
@commands `/ccaltime date`; `/time add 24000`; `/ccaltime date`; `/season get`
@pass day +1 in both, Serene Seasons agrees (SUN clock: `SereneSeasonsClockMixin`, `SeasonClock`)
@fails season clock back on Serene Seasons' tick counter: mixin gate or SeasonClock registration
@from batches/r1101/cs1_split.qb
> cetime date
> time add 24000
sleep 3
> cetime date
> season
reject Unknown command
look day +1 in both cetime lines, /season agrees

## SQ-CAL-06 | season and crop season tags
@group A
@commands `/locate biome #creativeengineering:seasons/arid`; place wheat at x y z, `/execute if block x y z #creativecalendar:crop_seasons/temperate run say temperate`; `/execute if block <glass> #sereneseasons:greenhouse_glass run say glass`
@pass a desert or badlands found; both `say` lines print (tags filled by the moved `sereneseasons/seasontags.js` and `cropseasontags.js`)
@fails Calendar server script tree missing from the jar, or `// requires: sereneseasons` skipped it
@from batches/r1101/cs1_split.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-17
> locate biome #creativeengineering:seasons/arid
waitlog (Located|Could not find) 180
expect (desert|badlands)
> forceload add 30 30
sleep 3
> setblock 30 -61 30 minecraft:farmland
> setblock 30 -60 30 minecraft:wheat
> execute if block 30 -60 30 #creativecalendar:crop_seasons/temperate run say CALTAG temperate
> setblock 32 -60 30 minecraft:glass
> execute if block 32 -60 30 #sereneseasons:greenhouse_glass run say CALTAG glass
expect CALTAG temperate
expect CALTAG glass

## SQ-CAL-07 | wine clock moves with the calendar
@group A
@commands `/wine time`; `/ccaltime date add 1 month`; `/wine time`; grep latest.log for `WineTime\|NoClassDefFound`
@pass the wine clock moves 8 days with the month (as SQ-TD-04); no class errors: the Vinery port's `PackTime` reads Calendar's `WineTime`
@fails CB built against the old Creative Common `time.WineTime`, or Calendar missing
@from batches/r1101/cs1_split.qb
> wine time
> cetime date add 1 month
> wine time
reject Unknown command
reject WineTime|NoClassDefFound
look wine clock moves 8 days with the month

